// Obfusku Canonical Example: Host and File System I/O
//
// Demonstrates:
// 1. Console printing via native `⌁↑ : ⌘ → ∅`.
// 2. Sandboxed file reading via native `⌁↓⌬ : ⌘ → ⌘`.
// 3. Sandboxed file writing via native `⌁↑⌬ : ⌘ → (⌘ → ∅)`.
// 4. Interactive input note: `⌁↓ : ∅ → ⌘` reads a line from stdin,
//    raising Failure("EOF", ...) when the input stream terminates.

// 1. Console printing
header ≔ "=== Obfusku I/O Subsystem ==="
loggedHeader ≔ ⌁↑(header)

// 2. Sandboxed file reading (scoped to the script directory)
initialData ≔ ⌁↓⌬("sample_message.txt")
loggedInitial ≔ ⌁↑(initialData)

// 3. Sandboxed file writing
// `⌁↑⌬` is curried: ⌁↑⌬(path)(content) -> ∅
writeStatus ≔ ⌁↑⌬("sample_message.txt")("Obfusku host I/O successfully verified.")

// 4. Verify written file contents
verifiedData ≔ ⌁↓⌬("sample_message.txt")
loggedVerified ≔ ⌁↑(verifiedData)

// Final returned result
result ≔ verifiedData
❧
